        <title type="html"><![CDATA[Using Semaphores to Control In-Flight Work]]></title>
        <id>https://asyncband.apache.org/blog/2026/10/14/choosing-the-right-primitive/</id>
        <link href="https://asyncband.apache.org/blog/2026/10/14/choosing-the-right-primitive/"/>
        <updated>2026-10-14T00:00:00.000Z</updated>
        <summary type="html"><![CDATA[Use Asyncband's Semaphore to share concurrency limits, keep permits with the resources they account for, and reserve capacity for work of different sizes.]]></summary>
        <content type="html"><![CDATA[<p>An asynchronous program can start work faster than the resources behind it can handle. Downloads compete for connections and bandwidth. Background jobs compete for CPU time. Buffered data occupies memory until its consumer finishes with it. A semaphore gives these operations a shared budget: work acquires permits before consuming capacity and returns them when that capacity becomes available again.</p>
<p>The useful questions are <strong>what one permit represents, which operations share the budget, and how long each operation holds its permits</strong>. This post works through those choices with Asyncband's <a href="https://docs.rs/asyncband/0.7.3/asyncband/semaphore/struct.Semaphore.html" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class=""><code>Semaphore</code></a>, including how Apache OpenDAL and prek use it.</p>
<p><em>The Asyncband APIs below are from version 0.7.3, with the <code>semaphore</code> feature enabled. The HTTP example uses reqwest; the semaphore itself is runtime-independent.</em></p>
<h2 class="anchor anchorTargetStickyNavbar_zq6S" id="share-a-budget-across-operations">Share a budget across operations<a href="https://asyncband.apache.org/blog/2026/10/14/choosing-the-right-primitive/#share-a-budget-across-operations" class="hash-link" aria-label="Direct link to Share a budget across operations" title="Direct link to Share a budget across operations" translate="no">​</a></h2>
<p>Suppose a client should perform at most eight downloads at once. Create one <code>Semaphore::new(8)</code> and share it across the calls that consume that budget. Each download acquires one permit. When all eight are held, another acquisition waits asynchronously until capacity becomes available.</p>
<div class="language-rust codeBlockContainer_lkHg theme-code-block" style="--prism-color:#393A34;--prism-background-color:#f6f8fa"><div class="codeBlockContent_KnrP"><pre tabindex="0" class="prism-code language-rust codeBlock_FDzL thin-scrollbar" style="color:#393A34;background-color:#f6f8fa"><code class="codeBlockLines_pYqn"><div class="token-line" style="color:#393A34"><span class="token keyword" style="color:#00009f">use</span><span class="token plain"> </span><span class="token namespace" style="opacity:0.7">asyncband</span><span class="token namespace punctuation" style="opacity:0.7;color:#393A34">::</span><span class="token namespace" style="opacity:0.7">semaphore</span><span class="token namespace punctuation" style="opacity:0.7;color:#393A34">::</span><span class="token class-name">Semaphore</span><span class="token punctuation" style="color:#393A34">;</span><span class="token plain"></span><br></div><div class="token-line" style="color:#393A34"><span class="token plain" style="display:inline-block"></span><br></div><div class="token-line" style="color:#393A34"><span class="token plain"></span><span class="token keyword" style="color:#00009f">async</span><span class="token plain"> </span><span class="token keyword" style="color:#00009f">fn</span><span class="token plain"> </span><span class="token function-definition function" style="color:#d73a49">download</span><span class="token punctuation" style="color:#393A34">(</span><span class="token plain"></span><br></div><div class="token-line" style="color:#393A34"><span class="token plain">    client</span><span class="token punctuation" style="color:#393A34">:</span><span class="token plain"> </span><span class="token operator" style="color:#393A34">&amp;</span><span class="token namespace" style="opacity:0.7">reqwest</span><span class="token namespace punctuation" style="opacity:0.7;color:#393A34">::</span><span class="token class-name">Client</span><span class="token punctuation" style="color:#393A34">,</span><span class="token plain"></span><br></div><div class="token-line" style="color:#393A34"><span class="token plain">    slots</span><span class="token punctuation" style="color:#393A34">:</span><span class="token plain"> </span><span class="token operator" style="color:#393A34">&amp;</span><span class="token class-name">Semaphore</span><span class="token punctuation" style="color:#393A34">,</span><span class="token plain"></span><br></div><div class="token-line" style="color:#393A34"><span class="token plain">    url</span><span class="token punctuation" style="color:#393A34">:</span><span class="token plain"> </span><span class="token operator" style="color:#393A34">&amp;</span><span class="token keyword" style="color:#00009f">str</span><span class="token punctuation" style="color:#393A34">,</span><span class="token plain"></span><br></div><div class="token-line" style="color:#393A34"><span class="token plain"></span><span class="token punctuation" style="color:#393A34">)</span><span class="token plain"> </span><span class="token punctuation" style="color:#393A34">-&gt;</span><span class="token plain"> </span><span class="token class-name">Result</span><span class="token operator" style="color:#393A34">&lt;</span><span class="token class-name">Vec</span><span class="token operator" style="color:#393A34">&lt;</span><span class="token keyword" style="color:#00009f">u8</span><span class="token operator" style="color:#393A34">&gt;</span><span class="token punctuation" style="color:#393A34">,</span><span class="token plain"> </span><span class="token namespace" style="opacity:0.7">reqwest</span><span class="token namespace punctuation" style="opacity:0.7;color:#393A34">::</span><span class="token class-name">Error</span><span class="token operator" style="color:#393A34">&gt;</span><span class="token plain"> </span><span class="token punctuation" style="color:#393A34">{</span><span class="token plain"></span><br></div><div class="token-line" style="color:#393A34"><span class="token plain">    </span><span class="token keyword" style="color:#00009f">let</span><span class="token plain"> _permit </span><span class="token operator" style="color:#393A34">=</span><span class="token plain"> slots</span><span class="token punctuation" style="color:#393A34">.</span><span class="token function" style="color:#d73a49">acquire</span><span class="token punctuation" style="color:#393A34">(</span><span class="token number" style="color:#36acaa">1</span><span class="token punctuation" style="color:#393A34">)</span><span class="token punctuation" style="color:#393A34">.</span><span class="token keyword" style="color:#00009f">await</span><span class="token punctuation" style="color:#393A34">;</span><span class="token plain"></span><br></div><div class="token-line" style="color:#393A34"><span class="token plain">    </span><span class="token keyword" style="color:#00009f">let</span><span class="token plain"> response </span><span class="token operator" style="color:#393A34">=</span><span class="token plain"> client</span><span class="token punctuation" style="color:#393A34">.</span><span class="token function" style="color:#d73a49">get</span><span class="token punctuation" style="color:#393A34">(</span><span class="token plain">url</span><span class="token punctuation" style="color:#393A34">)</span><span class="token punctuation" style="color:#393A34">.</span><span class="token function" style="color:#d73a49">send</span><span class="token punctuation" style="color:#393A34">(</span><span class="token punctuation" style="color:#393A34">)</span><span class="token punctuation" style="color:#393A34">.</span><span class="token keyword" style="color:#00009f">await</span><span class="token operator" style="color:#393A34">?</span><span class="token punctuation" style="color:#393A34">.</span><span class="token function" style="color:#d73a49">error_for_status</span><span class="token punctuation" style="color:#393A34">(</span><span class="token punctuation" style="color:#393A34">)</span><span class="token operator" style="color:#393A34">?</span><span class="token punctuation" style="color:#393A34">;</span><span class="token plain"></span><br></div><div class="token-line" style="color:#393A34"><span class="token plain">    </span><span class="token class-name">Ok</span><span class="token punctuation" style="color:#393A34">(</span><span class="token plain">response</span><span class="token punctuation" style="color:#393A34">.</span><span class="token function" style="color:#d73a49">bytes</span><span class="token punctuation" style="color:#393A34">(</span><span class="token punctuation" style="color:#393A34">)</span><span class="token punctuation" style="color:#393A34">.</span><span class="token keyword" style="color:#00009f">await</span><span class="token operator" style="color:#393A34">?</span><span class="token punctuation" style="color:#393A34">.</span><span class="token function" style="color:#d73a49">to_vec</span><span class="token punctuation" style="color:#393A34">(</span><span class="token punctuation" style="color:#393A34">)</span><span class="token punctuation" style="color:#393A34">)</span><span class="token plain"></span><br></div><div class="token-line" style="color:#393A34"><span class="token plain"></span><span class="token punctuation" style="color:#393A34">}</span><br></div></code></pre></div></div>
<p><code>acquire</code> returns a guard. Keeping that guard in <code>_permit</code> holds the slot through the download, including reading the response body. Returning from the function drops the guard and gives the slot back, including on an error. There is no separate success or error branch that needs to release it manually.</p>
<p>The semaphore must live outside the individual calls. Creating a new semaphore inside <code>download</code> would give every call its own eight-slot budget. An <code>Arc&lt;Semaphore&gt;</code> lets independently owned tasks share the same budget; each task can borrow it for <code>acquire</code> or use <code>acquire_owned</code> when the permit itself must own a reference to the semaphore.</p>
<p>This is useful when work comes from several places. Apache OpenDAL's <a href="https://github.com/apache/opendal/blob/ee8be2353d6af6152f6293cb8ac0b4d3d7a234d7/core/layers/concurrent-limit/src/lib.rs" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class=""><code>ConcurrentLimitLayer</code></a> lets multiple operators share an Asyncband semaphore. The hook runner <a href="https://github.com/j178/prek/blob/735c452028a698ce99ae5821dda9baedd0e07037/crates/prek/src/cli/run/run.rs" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="">prek</a> similarly passes one semaphore through project runs to limit concurrent hook execution. The scope of the shared semaphore determines the scope of the limit.</p>
<p>Eight slots limit simultaneous downloads. The number completed per second still depends on their duration. A policy expressed in requests per second needs a time-based rate limiter.</p>
<h2 class="anchor anchorTargetStickyNavbar_zq6S" id="keep-the-permit-with-the-resource">Keep the permit with the resource<a href="https://asyncband.apache.org/blog/2026/10/14/choosing-the-right-primitive/#keep-the-permit-with-the-resource" class="hash-link" aria-label="Direct link to Keep the permit with the resource" title="Direct link to Keep the permit with the resource" translate="no">​</a></h2>
<p>In the example above, the download ends when the response body has been read. A streaming API has a different lifetime: it can return a response while the caller is still receiving its body. Releasing a permit when the response is returned would leave that later transfer outside the budget.</p>
<p>OpenDAL handles this at its <a href="https://github.com/apache/opendal/blob/ee8be2353d6af6152f6293cb8ac0b4d3d7a234d7/core/layers/concurrent-limit/src/lib.rs#L191" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="">HTTP transport boundary</a>. When an HTTP concurrency limit is configured, it acquires a permit before sending the request and moves the permit into a wrapper around the response body stream. The stream holds the permit until it is dropped. If sending the request fails, the local permit is dropped instead.</p>
<p>That ownership pattern also applies to a returned buffer or a queued job: put the permit in the object that owns the charged resource. If ownership moves to another task, move the permit with it. The function that acquired the permit may return long before the resource is released.</p>
<p>The download example's returned <code>Vec&lt;u8&gt;</code> illustrates the boundary. Its slot covers the transfer, but the caller can retain the downloaded bytes afterward. Limiting transfers alone does not bound retained memory.</p>
<h2 class="anchor anchorTargetStickyNavbar_zq6S" id="charge-for-the-size-of-the-work">Charge for the size of the work<a href="https://asyncband.apache.org/blog/2026/10/14/choosing-the-right-primitive/#charge-for-the-size-of-the-work" class="hash-link" aria-label="Direct link to Charge for the size of the work" title="Direct link to Charge for the size of the work" translate="no">​</a></h2>
<p>A permit can represent a byte of capacity instead of one operation. This matters when a small buffer and a large buffer should consume different amounts of a shared budget.</p>
<p>Here is a standalone example of a fixed payload budget. It reserves capacity before allocating a buffer and keeps the reservation with the returned value:</p>
